    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm doing an accessibility audit for a fintech app we're launching. can you give me a quick checklist for WCAG 2.1 compliance focusing on color contrast ratios and screen reader compatibility? thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For color contrast, ensure all text and interactive elements meet a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for standard text and 3:1 for large text, as per WCAG 2.1 AA. Regarding screen reader compatibility, verify that all images have descriptive `alt` text, and that form fields and interactive elements are correctly labeled using accessible names. Also, ensure sufficient focus indication is visible for keyboard-only users.",
